('I5','Actual rational cutoffs for a proper height, avoiding max(gamma-j,-c).',r'''Choose RATIONAL c with H0=gamma0+c>=0 everywhere; gamma0 is proper and has finite lower bound by vertex-plus-recession decomposition. Define q_j=max(gamma0-j,-c) for positive integer j; it is an ACTUAL rational-affine PA_R PC function on RATIONAL geometry, since all its data are rational. It has the same recession as gamma0. Now theta_j=gamma'+epsilon*q_j is ACTUAL relative PA_R PC for ORIGINAL gamma on a rational refinement, satisfies theta_j<=gamma and gamma-theta_j=epsilon*min(H0,j). Crucially max(gamma-j,-c) itself is NOT declared rational-carrier PA when gamma has irrational coefficients. Let J0=integral H0 MA(gamma), finite because the actual finite raw reference measure is supported on finitely many finite vertices. S262 Lemma9 bounded-difference IBP and positivity compare the two TRUE products for a tuple with max_i||a_i-gamma||<=C. In each telescoping term the bounded factor a_i-gamma is at most C and the difference of the two positive mixed products has total variation at most2M. Thus epsilon*integral min(H0,j) MA(a)<=epsilon*J0+2dCM, uniformly in j. Monotone truncation gives integral H0 MA(a)<=K_C,0=(2d/epsilon)CM+J0. All products used here are finite genuinely defined PA products; no unregularizable test receives an operator. This is an exact height bound for THIS rational-component height, not the older K_C formula for H=gamma+c. The reference and raw mass remain unchanged.'''),
('I6','Actual arbitrary-reference mixed completion, with correct uniformities.',r'''For any uniform/decreasing real relative PA approximation family to an endpoint tuple, compact-test estimateI4 and controlled-support density give Cauchy evaluations on all C_c tests. The complete positive-functional Radon construction in accepted S262 Lemma12 yields a positive Radon limit. Each fixed uniform family has bounded relative norms, soI5 gives common proper-height tails and prevents loss of raw mass. Compact cutoffs then give all-C_b convergence and exact mass M;I4 compares arbitrary families to establish sequence independence. For EVERY completed tuple with bound C, choose approximants with bound C+o(1); pass compact height truncations and then increase them to obtain the SAME exact K_C,0 for ALL tuples in the ENTIRE fixed-C family. Hence weak C_b and BL uniform continuity hold ONLY on each fixed-C family; global vague uniform continuity holds without fixed C. Finite compact BL test nets and radius-one neighborhoods give respectively fixed-family BL uniformity and ordinary weak C_b continuity for sequences AND nets. Symmetry, locality and raw PA agreement pass as in S262. Genuine decreasing extraction uses errors2^-n and rational constant shifts4*2^-n, so the declared uniform closure equals its actual decreasing approximation domain. No assertion that all CONT PC functions are regularizable in dimension>=2 is made. This new theorem closes the arbitrary-irrational-reference limitation of this REAL mixed completion, not the full original contact classification.'''),
